// Rule 1: a `slot` names the storage an `out` parameter is about to fill, and that is ALL it does. A hole
// filled by ASSIGNMENT is not a slot — it is a local whose value arrives one line late, and `T x = …;` says
// so with the value in hand. This is the habit the campaign removed: `slot` was the nearest keyword when
// implicit default construction went away, and 73% of its uses were construction rather than holes.
// (Branch initialization has a stronger spelling still — `match` and the ternary both build a value.)
fn int32 main() {
    slot int32 area;
    area = 6 * 7;      // ERROR: an assignment does not fill a slot
    return area;
}
